MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next step because it would let my existing Echo speakers and display control another household device.",
    "The memory cards fit my card reader and older removable-storage use, provided they are compatible; the HDMI cable also fits my TV equipment, although I would need a reason to replace or extend a cable."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "More Fire TV sticks do not solve a current need because I recently acquired a 4K Max bundle, and the older or HD versions offer little reason to switch.",
    "The first-generation Echo Show feels redundant after my second-generation Show and stand, while the older tablet and wired earbuds have no clear purpose in my recent purchases."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to be taken as a reason to offer more Alexa devices, even when they repeat something I already have.",
    "My history of buying electronics seems to count too broadly: a useful computer accessory does not mean I currently need earbuds, a tablet, or another streaming player."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they show which needs are already covered; a compatible addition is more appealing than an older replacement.",
    "I need a specific use for an accessory: I would choose only one compatible memory card, and a ten-foot HDMI cable would matter only if I needed that length."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my home-electronics interests but miss that I currently want useful additions to equipment I own rather than more devices serving the same purpose."
}
